      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "RAY COOKE AUCTIONEERS are delighted to introduce 10 Moy Glas Drive to the Lucan market. This beautiful semi-detatched family home consists of 3 bedrooms, 3 bathrooms and an built shed to the rear with electricity and plumbing. This property is nicely nestled in a quiet development with a number of amenities in the area including Lucan Village, Liffey Valley Shopping Centre, Griffeen Valley Park and the new Lucan Swimming Pool and Gym. There are several primary and secondary schools, supermarkets, shops, restaurants, bars, and cafes all in close proximity. The area is well catered for by public transportation with Kishoge train station being a 5-minute drive away and several bus stops in the locality. The N4 is minutes away and provides easy access to the M50, Dublin Airport, and Dublin City Centre.\n\nBright, spacious and light filled interior living accommodation of c. 100 sq.m comprises of an inviting entrance hallway with a guest w.c, and a cosy lounge room to the front. The downstairs further consists of an open plan kitchen/ diner with an additional utility room. Upstairs boasts a main family bathroom and three spacious bedrooms with the master benefiting of an ensuite. Externally to the rear you will find a low maintenance rear garden comleted in 2022 with a sunny SOUTH WEST origentation for the sunshine all throughout the day. The rear garden also boasts a built shed for storage with access to electricity and plumbing which can be used for a variety of uses in the future. Externally to the front you will find an extra wide front driveway for off-street parking which has been completed in 2020.\n\nNo.10 comes to the market in fantastic condition throughout and boasts gas fired central heating, double glazed windows, utility room, built shed, XL front driveway, attic with stira ladder and a SOUTH WEST rear garden. This fine family home is ideal for first time buyers and families looking to trade up. Early viewing is highly advised, Call Ray Cooke Auctioneers for further information or to arrange viewing on 01 403 0720.\n\nFeatures:\n-3 Bed/ 3 bath\n-TURN KEY Semi-deatched Family home\n-Built shed to rear with electricity & plumbing\n-SOUTH WEST rear garden\n-Lanscaped rear garden completed in 2022\n-Landscaped front driveway completed in 2020\n-Gas fired central heating\n-Double glazed windows\n-Light filled interior\n-Wide front driveway for off street parking\n-Quiet development\n-Spacious room proportions\n-Within easy access to a host of shops and supermarkets\n-A host of transport links at your doorstep\n-Kishoge train station only a 5-minute drive away\n-Liffey Valley Shopping Centre within easy reach\n-Viewing highly advised!\n\nDirections:\n\nEircode = K78 T997"
      },
      {
